                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "17921642",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198059561891",
                            "num_reviews": 416,
                            "playtime_forever": 93,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 93,
                            "last_played": 1441583502
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "D.G.U. is a game I really want to like. It has all the personality and charm that you would want in a game like this. Making fun of pop culture references and being completely silly in nature. The gameplay is rather simplistic but for an adventure that is perfectly fine. The best way to put it is that the tone of D.G.U. is superb. From graphics to music, everything is adorable and strange. Where things fall apart are the technical aspects of this title. From resolution bugs, extremely long load times and lack of cohesive gameplay. I felt I spent more time battling the bugs and looking at loading screens then actually playing the game. When the game did manage to work well, the framerate would suddenly tank for no reason at all. The optimization needs to be fixed for this to be an enjoyable title because the issues suck the fun out of the game. Now the question stands, does the good outweigh the bad? I would say yes, I wanted to see more about the game, it's puzzles, humor, and gameplay. I still do, however the issues make it a sour experience. So I would recommend this game if you truly love the humor, genre, and don't mind dealing with optimization issues. \n\nI made a video review to show off some of the features and gameplay of this game!\nhttps://youtu.be/YjEDXgZ20Lg\nI hope you enjoy!\nMartyr",
                        "timestamp_created": 1441590922,
